summary:
  Verdicts given while an alarm rang double the waits of the listening after it.

history:
  Outside an alarm every verdict doubles the wait before the next, up to
  five minutes, until ten minutes of sound forgive it. An alarm's verdicts
  do not double and may be several; counted, the first silence of the station
  the listener puts on after getting up would stand for 40 or 80 s before
  anything was done about it.

target:
  package/contents/ui/StandWatch.qml

find:
          if (!waking) _strikes++;

replace:
          _strikes++;

expect:
  Killed by tst_standwatch::test_what_an_alarm_went_through_is_not_held_against_the_listening_after_it.
  Line-neutral.
